  "stem": "A point mass oscillates along the x-axis according to the law $x = x_{0}\\cos (\\omega t - \\frac{\\pi}{4})$. If the acceleration of the particle is written as $a = A\\cos (\\omega t + \\delta)$, then:",
  "options": {
    "A": "$A = x_{0};\\ \\delta = - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
    "B": "$A = x_{0}\\omega^{2};\\ \\delta = \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
    "C": "$A = x_{0}\\omega^{2};\\ \\delta = - \\frac{\\pi}{4}$",
    "D": "$A = x_{0}\\omega^{2};\\ \\delta = \\frac{3\\pi}{4}$"
  },
  "answer": {
